Z||000000||U Wanna Race||10-15-2001||11:56 AM||||The temp gauge seems to be working fine, the needle goes up smoothly while driving and acts normal.  But the needle never drops below 220, even if it is a cold day or when you start it up from being untouched for hours.  Why would this happen?||||reg||1
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||10-15-2001||01:18 PM||||is it always at 220 or once it gets that high it wont come down.  if it gets taht hight then doesnt come down i would check the radiator first because its easy to check.  when the car is hot open the hood and put your hand over the radiator.  make sure you unplug the fan!!!! dont want ya to lose any fingers.  if the temp on the radiator has any "cold" spots your rad. is clogged and needs flushed or replaced.  if it is consistantly hot over the entire rad. then i would check the t-stat or water pump next.  good luck.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||U Wanna Race||10-15-2001||05:35 PM||||It never drops below 220.  Its like it treats the 220 as the 0 mark.||||reg||9
